// Every number here is the output of the quickstart or a published report.
import { RELEASE, RELEASE_URL, REPO, REPORTS } from '../consts';
---
<div class="home">
	<section class="hero">
		<span class="eyebrow">Open-source RADIUS server</span>
		<h1>Network logins and usage records<br />that survive a server failure.</h1>
		<p class="lead">
			radiusward authenticates Wi‑Fi, VPN and subscriber sessions against your users file, SQL database or Active
			Directory — and stores every session record on three servers before it answers, so a crash never loses a
			record or counts one twice.
		</p>
		<div class="actions">
			<a class="btn btn-primary" href="/docs/start/quickstart/">Try it in 10 minutes →</a>
			<a class="btn" href="/reliability/">See how it fails — and recovers</a>
		</div>
		<p class="meta">
			<span>Apache-2.0</span><span>Docker · Kubernetes · systemd · Amazon ECS</span><span><a href={RELEASE_URL}>{RELEASE.label} {RELEASE.tag}</a></span>
		</p>

		<figure class="terminal" aria-label="The quickstart on a laptop: start the cluster, then kill the leader under load">
			<div class="bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><em>the quickstart, on a laptop</em></div>
			<pre><code><span class="p">$</span> docker compose -f deploy/compose/compose.yaml up -d --wait
<span class="o">✔ node-0  node-1  node-2  server-a   server-b   postgres   healthy</span>
<span class="p">$</span> deploy/compose/demo-failover.sh
<span class="o">load: 10,000 sessions, 2,000 requests/s for 25 s
kill -9 of the leader: node-2
new leader: node-0
verifying every acknowledged event against the replicated state...
sessions=10000
<b>lost=0</b></span></code></pre>
			<figcaption>What the <a href="/docs/start/quickstart/">quickstart</a> prints: three cluster members and two RADIUS servers, the leader killed while 10,000 sessions report in, and every acknowledged record still there.</figcaption>
		</figure>
	</section>

	<section class="block">
		<span class="eyebrow">Built for</span>
		<h2>Networks where the session record matters.</h2>
		<div class="three">
			<article>
				<h3>Internet and wireless providers</h3>
				<p>
					Your invoice is built on session records. A RADIUS server outage, a lost Stop, or a retransmission counted
					twice turns into a billing dispute. radiusward keeps every record on three servers and counts each session
					once — through outages and failovers.
				</p>
			</article>
			<article>
				<h3>Campus and enterprise networks</h3>
				<p>
					Wi‑Fi and wired 802.1X, VPN: certificates or passwords against Active Directory, LDAP or SQL, a second factor
					if you want one. Logins keep working when a server is lost, and the records of who was online when are not.
				</p>
			</article>
			<article>
				<h3>Platform teams</h3>
				<p>
					One container image, a Helm chart tested every night under failures, Prometheus metrics with dashboards and
					alerts, a continuous backup — and no appliance. Runs on Kubernetes, plain hosts, or Amazon ECS.
				</p>
			</article>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="block problem">
		<span class="eyebrow">The problem with RADIUS accounting</span>
		<h2>Session records (RADIUS accounting) are easy to lose and easy to double-count.</h2>
		<div class="pairs">
			<div>
				<h3>Lost in an outage</h3>
				<p class="pain">A device sends its session records to the RADIUS server and retries for a while. If the server is down for longer than that, the records — the usage you bill — are gone.</p>
				<p class="fix"><strong>radiusward:</strong> a record is confirmed only after it is written to disk on two of three servers. A crash of any one of them loses nothing that was confirmed.</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<h3>Counted twice on a retry</h3>
				<p class="pain">A device that gets no answer in time sends the same record again — often to its secondary server. A server that does not recognise the retry stores the session twice and inflates the usage.</p>
				<p class="fix"><strong>radiusward:</strong> retries are recognised by session, not by server — also after a failover, also through the other RADIUS server — and counted once.</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<h3>Torn apart by a failover</h3>
				<p class="pain">With a primary and a secondary server, the Start lands on one and the Stop on the other. Reconciling them afterwards is where the ghost sessions and the billing errors come from.</p>
				<p class="fix"><strong>radiusward:</strong> all RADIUS servers write to the same replicated state, so a session is one session wherever its records arrived. A failed leader is replaced in about two seconds.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
		<p class="more-row"><a href="/docs/reliability/accounting-contract/">Exactly what a confirmation guarantees →</a></p>
	</section>

	<section class="block">
		<span class="eyebrow">Works with what you have</span>
		<h2>Your users, your devices, your database.</h2>
		<dl class="chips">
			<div><dt>Your users</dt><dd><span>users file</span><span>SQL</span><span>LDAP</span><span>Active Directory</span><span>Active Directory over Netlogon</span></dd></div>
			<div><dt>Your devices</dt><dd><span>access points and switches (802.1X)</span><span>VPN concentrators</span><span>broadband gateways (BNG)</span><span>captive portals</span><span>private LTE/5G Wi‑Fi offload</span></dd></div>
			<div><dt>Methods</dt><dd><span>EAP‑TLS</span><span>PEAP</span><span>TTLS</span><span>TEAP</span><span>EAP‑pwd</span><span>EAP‑SIM/AKA</span><span>PAP</span><span>CHAP</span><span>MS‑CHAP</span><span>TOTP</span></dd></div>
			<div><dt>On the wire</dt><dd><span>UDP</span><span>RadSec (TLS)</span><span>DTLS</span><span>TCP</span><span>proxying to other RADIUS servers</span><span>CoA and Disconnect</span></dd></div>
			<div><dt>Your records go to</dt><dd><span>PostgreSQL</span><span>JSON-lines files</span><span>another RADIUS server</span></dd></div>
			<div><dt>Runs on</dt><dd><span>Docker</span><span>Kubernetes (Helm)</span><span>systemd</span><span>Amazon ECS</span></dd></div>
		</dl>
		<p class="more-row"><a href="/product/">All capabilities →</a> <a href="/docs/authentication/choosing-a-method/">Which method fits your clients →</a></p>
	</section>

	<section class="block">
		<span class="eyebrow">See it survive</span>
		<h2>Tested against the failures that happen, every night.</h2>
		<div class="three">
			<a href={`${REPORTS}/linux/`}>
				<strong>Power loss, partitions, full disks ↗</strong>
				<span>All three servers lose power at once under load; the network splits; a disk fills up; the database goes away. Nightly, on Linux, with the results published.</span>
			</a>
			<a href={`${REPORTS}/k8s/`}>
				<strong>Kubernetes chaos ↗</strong>
				<span>The leader killed, members and RADIUS servers rolled, a disk replaced, a lost quorum restored from the backup — under accounting and login load, through a load balancer.</span>
			</a>
			<a href={`${REPORTS}/benchmarks/`}>
				<strong>Benchmarks ↗</strong>
				<span>How much it carries and how fast it answers, with the machine and the method stated. The leader killed under load in every run: nothing lost so far.</span>
			</a>
		</div>
		<p class="honest">
			radiusward is young: a release candidate, automated tests on every change, and published results — not yet a
			production track record, device certifications or an independent security audit.
			<a href="/docs/reliability/evidence/">What the evidence shows, and what it does not →</a>
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="band">
		<div>
			<h2>Open source. Built in the open.</h2>
			<p>
				Apache-2.0. The code, every design decision, the tests and their results are public — and everything on this
				page can be reproduced on your laptop.
			</p>
		</div>
		<div class="band-actions">
			<a class="btn btn-primary" href="/docs/start/quickstart/">Try it in 10 minutes →</a>
			<a class="btn" href={REPO}>GitHub ↗</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</div>

<style>
	.home { --gap: clamp(3.5rem, 2rem + 4vw, 6rem); }
	.home :global(a) { text-decoration: none; }
	.eyebrow { display: block; margin-bottom: 0.9rem; color: var(--color-primary); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
	h1, h2, h3 { color: var(--color-text); letter-spacing: -0.03em; line-height: 1.12; margin: 0; }
	h2 { font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 1.2rem + 1vw, 2.1rem); max-width: 30ch; }
	h3 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
	p { margin: 0; }

	.hero { padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 1.5rem + 4vw, 5rem) var(--gap); text-align: center; }
	.hero .eyebrow { margin-bottom: 1.2rem; }
	.hero h1 { font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 1.2rem + 3vw, 4rem); line-height: 1.06; letter-spacing: -0.045em; max-width: 22ch; margin-inline: auto; }
	.lead { margin: 1.4rem auto 0; max-width: 62ch; color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: 1.1rem; }
	.actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; gap: 0.8rem; margin-top: 1.8rem; }
	.meta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; gap: 0.4rem 1rem; margin-top: 1.4rem; color: var(--color-text-faint); font-family: var(--font-code); font-size: 0.78rem; }
	.meta > * + *::before { content: '/'; margin-right: 1rem; }
	.meta a { color: var(--color-primary); }

	.terminal { margin: 2.8rem auto 0; max-width: 46rem; text-align: left; border-radius: var(--radius-md); background: var(--color-code-bg); color: var(--color-code-text); box-shadow: var(--shadow); overflow: hidden; }
	.bar { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.45rem; padding: 0.6rem 0.9rem; border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(255 255 255 / 0.1); font-size: 0.75rem; }
	.bar span { width: 0.7rem; height: 0.7rem; border-radius: 50%; background: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.18); }
	.bar em { margin-left: 0.5rem; font-style: normal; color: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.55); }
	.terminal pre { margin: 0; padding: 1rem 1.2rem 1.2rem; overflow-x: auto; font-family: var(--font-code); font-size: 0.86rem; line-height: 1.65; }
	.terminal .p { color: var(--color-primary); }
	.terminal .o { color: rgb(232 238 234 / 0.75); }
	.terminal b { color: #7fd8a0; }
	.terminal figcaption { padding: 0.8rem 1.2rem 1rem; border-top: 1px solid rgb(255 255 255 / 0.1); color: rgb(232 238 234 / 0.7); font-size: 0.82rem; line-height: 1.5; }
	.terminal figcaption a { color: #a9d8d3; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 0.2em; }

	.block { margin-bottom: var(--gap); }
	.block > h2 { margin-bottom: 1.8rem; }
	.three { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1.2rem; }
	.three > * { display: block; padding: 1.4rem 1.6rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: var(--radius-md); background: var(--color-surface); color: var(--color-text); }
	.three a:hover { border-color: var(--color-primary); }
	.three p, .three span { color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; }
	.three strong { display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; font-size: 1.1rem; }
	.three span { display: block; }

	.pairs { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1.2rem; }
	.pairs > div { padding: 1.4rem 1.6rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-left: 4px solid var(--color-caution); border-radius: var(--radius-md); background: var(--color-surface); }
	.pain { color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; }
	.fix { margin-top: 0.9rem; padding-top: 0.9rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-divider); font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); }
	.fix strong { color: var(--color-primary); }
	.more-row { margin-top: 1.2rem; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem 1.6rem; font-size: 0.95rem; }
	.more-row a { color: var(--color-primary); font-weight: 700; }

	.chips { display: grid; gap: 0.9rem; margin: 0; }
	.chips > div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 11rem 1fr; gap: 0.6rem 1rem; align-items: start; padding-bottom: 0.9rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-divider); }
	.chips dt { font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.95rem; padding-top: 0.25rem; }
	.chips dd { margin: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.4rem; }
	.chips dd span { padding: 0.2rem 0.65rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 999rem; background: var(--color-surface); font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); }

	.honest { margin-top: 1.4rem; max-width: 80ch; color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; }
	.honest a { color: var(--color-primary); font-weight: 700; }

	.band { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto; gap: 1.5rem; align-items: center; padding: clamp(1.4rem, 1rem + 1.5vw, 2.4rem); margin-bottom: 2rem; border-radius: var(--radius-md); background: var(--color-primary-tint); }
	.band p { margin-top: 0.5rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); max-width: 60ch; }
	.band-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.8rem; }

	@media (max-width: 56rem) {
		.three, .pairs { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
		.band { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
		.chips > div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.4rem; }
	}
</style>
